  "note": "Apple's default macOS and iOS wallpapers as light/dark pairs, and the Mac OS X Nature desktop pictures as single photographs. Apple retains rights to this artwork; it is committed here for a personal site, not licensed onward. The archives the files were pulled from (ryOS included, which is AGPL-3.0) do not license Apple's images either, and their repository licenses are not asserted to do so. Resolution rule: every committed full-size file is the smallest cover of a 2560x1600 viewport at 2x (5120x3200 device pixels), never upscaled past the source. A matching @1x cover (.1x.webp) ships beside it whenever that is smaller, so a 1x display does not download the retina file. iOS 27 (1320x2868), iOS 18 (1480x3192 / 1661x3600), iOS 17 (2048x2048) and portrait iPadOS 26/27 (2064x2752) fell short of a 1x 2560x1600 cover and were left out; iPadOS 26 is the landscape home-screen still. Derivatives: graphic release pairs are WebP q80; photographs WebP q95 with 4:4:4 chroma (q90 if a file would exceed ~1.8MB per 2560x1600 megapixel — the q75 encode crushed smooth skies); thumbnails at most 480px at q72. Nothing is cropped: every committed file keeps its source aspect. The Nature photographs carry Photoshop timestamps from August 2007, the Mac OS X Leopard cycle; the individual releases they shipped with are not verified. Clown Fish and Ladybug were dropped from the catalog. High-resolution originals were collected from: wallpapers.poutanen.dev (macOS 6K graphic pairs Tahoe–Big Sur, iOS 13 3208² / iOS 14 3072²), 4kwallpapers.com (Golden Gate native 4480x3088 — the 6016x4147 '6K' files are a uniform upscale of that pair and are not used — Catalina 6016x6016, Mojave 5120x2880, iOS 15 2916x2916, iPadOS 18 3840x2668), static.applewalls.com (iPadOS 26 landscape 2752x2064), LAYTAT/macOS-Wallpapers and benediktkr/Deeeee-macOS-Wallpapers (untouched /System/Desktop Pictures dumps), 512pixels.net (classic defaults; 6K files there are hand-upscales and are not used). Portrait iPhone lock-screens never cover 2560x1600.",
